<problem>
<!-- <title>Secant and differentiability of absolute value, worksheet</title> -->

<setup>

<function name="f" variables="x" symbolic="true">abs(x)</function>
<function name="secant_slope" variables="a h">($$f(a+h)-$$f(a))/h</function>
<number name="slope_n05_1">$$secant_slope(-0.5, 1)</number>
<number name="slope_n05_n1">$$secant_slope(-0.5, -1)</number>
<number name="slope_n05_01">$$secant_slope(-0.5, 0.1)</number>
<number name="slope_n05_001">$$secant_slope(-0.5, 0.01)</number>
<number name="slope_n05_n01">$$secant_slope(-0.5, -0.1)</number>
<number name="slope_n05_n001">$$secant_slope(-0.5, -0.01)</number>
<number name="fprime_n05">$slope_n05_n001 </number>
<number name="slope_0_1">$$secant_slope(0, 1)</number>
<number name="slope_0_01">$$secant_slope(0, 0.1)</number>
<number name="slope_0_001">$$secant_slope(0, 0.01)</number>
<number name="slope_0_n1">$$secant_slope(0, -1)</number>
<number name="slope_0_n01">$$secant_slope(0, -0.1)</number>
<number name="slope_0_n001">$$secant_slope(0, -0.01)</number>

</setup>


<p>Let <m>f</m> be the absolute value function <m>f(x)=|x|</m>.  We'll explore where the function is differentiable (i.e., where the derivative exists).  The function is differentiable at the point <m>a</m> if the limit
<me>\frac{df}{dx}\biggr|_{x=a} = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h} = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{|a+h|-|a|}{h}</me>
exists.  For the limit to exist, the expression must approach the same value for both positive and negative <m>h</m>.
</p>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>For <m>a=-0.5</m>, calculate the slopes <m>\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}</m> of the secant lines for:
</p>
<p>

<m>h=1</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_n05_1 </award>
</answer>
, <m>h= -1</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_n05_n1 </award>
</answer>

</p>
<p>

<m>h=0.1</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_n05_01 </award>
</answer>
, <m>h= -0.1</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_n05_n01 </award>
</answer>

</p>
<p>

<m>h=0.01</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_n05_001 </award>
</answer>
, <m>h= -0.01</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_n05_n001 </award>
</answer>
</p>

<p>Does the derivative <m>\frac{df}{dx}\Bigr|_{x=-0.5}</m> exist?  
<answer inline="true">
<choiceInput>
<choice credit="1">yes</choice>
<choice>no</choice>
</choiceInput>
</answer>
 If so, what is its value?  
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$fprime_n05 </award>
</answer>
 Is the function differentiable at <m>x=-0.5</m>? 
<answer inline="true">
<choiceInput>
<choice credit="1">yes</choice>
<choice>no</choice>
</choiceInput>
</answer>
</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>For <m>a=0</m>, calculate the slopes <m>\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}</m> of the secant lines for:
</p>
<p>

<m>h=1</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_0_1 </award>
</answer>
, <m>h= -1</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_0_n1 </award>
</answer>

</p>
<p>

<m>h=0.1</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_0_01 </award>
</answer>
, <m>h= -0.1</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_0_n01 </award>
</answer>

</p>
<p>

<m>h=0.01</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_0_001 </award>
</answer>
, <m>h= -0.01</m>: 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="numbers">$slope_0_n001 </award>
</answer>
</p>

<p>Does the derivative <m>\frac{df}{dx}\Bigr|_{x=0}</m> exist?  
<answer inline="true">
<choiceInput>
<choice credit="1">no</choice>
<choice>yes</choice>
</choiceInput>
</answer>
  Is the function differentiable at <m>x=0</m>? 
<answer inline="true">
<choiceInput>
<choice credit="1">no</choice>
<choice>yes</choice>
</choiceInput>
</answer>
</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Sketch a graph of the function <m>f(x)</m> and its derivative <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m> in four steps: </p>
  <ul>
    
    <li>Step 1: Move the $absVertex.styleDescription points so that the $absRay1.styleDescription lines represent the graph of <m>f(x)</m>.      
  
   
<graph size="medium" xmin="-4.5" xmax="4.5" ymin="-4.5" ymax="4.5" showNavigation="false" grid="true" identicalAxisScales="true" name="graph3a">

  
  <point name="absVertex" styleNumber="3" x="1" y="1">
    <attractToGrid />
  </point>
  
  <point name="abs1" x="-3" y="1" styleNumber="3">
    <attractToGrid />
  </point>
  
  <point name="abs2" x="2" y="1" styleNumber="3">
    <attractToGrid />
  </point>
  
  <ray fixed="true" name="absRay1" endpoint="$absVertex" through="$abs1" styleNumber="3" applyStyleToLabel="true">
    <label><m>f(x)</m></label>
  </ray>
  <ray fixed="true" name="absRay2" endpoint="$absVertex" through="$abs2" styleNumber="3" />
    

</graph>
      
<p>Graph of function: 
  <answer>
    <award>
      <when matchPartial="true">
        (<boolean>$absVertex=(0,0) and $ay1 > 0 and $ax1 = $ay1</boolean> and
        <boolean>$absVertex=(0,0) and $ay2 > 0 and $ax2 = -$ay2</boolean>)
        or
        (<boolean>$absVertex=(0,0) and $ay1 > 0 and $ax1 = -$ay1</boolean> and
        <boolean>$absVertex=(0,0) and $ay2 > 0 and $ax2 = $ay2</boolean>)     
      </when>
    </award>
    <considerAsResponses>
      $absVertex $abs1 $abs2
    </considerAsResponses>
  </answer>
</p>
    </li>

<li>Step 2: Identify and add a red square at all locations on the graph of <m>f(x)</m> where the derivative fails. You can generate as many red squares as you need using the "Add Point" and "Delete Point" buttons.

  <graph extend="$graph3a" name="graph3b">

  
  <repeatForSequence from="1" to="$n_nodiff" name="nodiff_points" valueName="v" indexName="i"><setup><number copy="$v" fixed="false" name="ref1" /></setup>
      <point stylenumber="2" x="$ref1-4" y="3">
        <attractToGrid /><constrainToGraph />
      </point>
    </repeatForSequence>
  </graph>
     
<p>Click <updateValue target="$n_nodiff" newValue="$n_nodiff+1">
  <label>Add Red Square</label>
</updateValue> and <updateValue target="$n_nodiff" newValue="$n_nodiff-1" disabled="$n_nodiff=0">
  <label>Delete Red Square</label>
</updateValue> to change the number of points and move them to the locations where <m>f(x)</m> is not differentiable.</p>

<number hide="true" name="n_nodiff">0</number>


<math hide="true" name="ax1" extend="$abs1.x" />
<math hide="true" name="ay1" extend="$abs1.y" />
<math hide="true" name="ax2" extend="$abs2.x" />
<math hide="true" name="ay2" extend="$abs2.y" />

<math hide="true" name="dtx1" extend="$derivThru1.x" />
<math hide="true" name="dty1" extend="$derivThru1.y" />
<math hide="true" name="dtx2" extend="$derivThru2.x" />
<math hide="true" name="dty2" extend="$derivThru2.y" />


<p>Point(s) of non-differentiability:  
<answer>
  <award referencesAreResponses="$nodiff_points"><when>
    <mathList>$nodiff_points</mathList> = (0,0)
  </when></award>
</answer>
</p>
</li>

<li>Step 3: Move the $derivThru1.styleDescription points so that the $derivRay1.styleDescription lines represent the graph of <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m>.

<graph extend="$graph3b" name="graph3c">

    <point name="derivThru1" x="-2" y="0">
    <attractToGrid includeGridlines="true" />
  </point>
  
  <endpoint name="derivEnd1" x="-1" y="0" switchable="true">
    <attractToGrid />
  </endpoint>
  
  <ray fixed="true" name="derivRay1" endpoint="$derivEnd1" through="$derivThru1" applyStyleToLabel="true">
    <label><m>\frac{df}{dx}</m></label>
  </ray>
   
  <endpoint name="derivEnd2" x="3" y="0" switchable="true">
    <attractToGrid />
  </endpoint>
  
  <point name="derivThru2" x="4" y="0">
    <attractToGrid includeGridlines="true" />
  </point>
  
  <ray fixed="true" name="derivRay2" endpoint="$derivEnd2" through="$derivThru2" applyStyleToLabel="true">
    <label><m>\frac{df}{dx}</m></label>
  </ray>

</graph>
  
<p>Graph of derivative:
  <answer>
    <award>
      <when matchPartial="true">
        (<boolean>$derivEnd1=(0,1) and $dtx1 > 0 and $dty1 = 1</boolean> and <boolean>$derivEnd2=(0,-1) and $dtx2 &lt; 0 and $dty2 = -1</boolean>) or
        (<boolean>$derivEnd1=(0,-1) and $dtx1 &lt; 0 and $dty1 = -1</boolean> and <boolean>$derivEnd2=(0,1) and $dtx2 > 0 and $dty2 = 1</boolean>)
      </when>
    </award>
    <considerAsResponses>
      $derivEnd1 $derivThru1 $derivEnd2 $derivThru2
    </considerAsResponses>
  </answer>
</p>
</li>
    

<li>Step 4: Click the $derivEnd1.styleDescriptionWithNoun (s) to toggle an open endpoint at any location(s) where the derivative function is not defined.
<p>Open endpoints of derivative:
  <answer>
    <award>
      <when matchPartial="true">
        $derivEnd1.open = true and $derivEnd2.open = true
      </when>
    </award>
    <considerAsResponses>
      $derivEnd1 $derivThru1 $derivEnd2 $derivThru2
    </considerAsResponses>
  </answer>
</p>
</li>
</ul>
</exercise>
  
<solution>


<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>For <m>a=-0.5</m>, the secant slopes are:
</p>
<p>

<m>h=1: $slope_n05_1 </m>, <m>h= -1: $slope_n05_n1 </m>
</p>
<p>

<m>h=0.1: $slope_n05_01 </m>, <m>h= -0.1: $slope_n05_n01 </m>
</p>
<p>

<m>h=0.01: $slope_n05_001 </m>, <m>h= -0.01: $slope_n05_n001 </m>
</p>

<p>The derivative exists at <m>a=-0.5</m>, i.e., the function is differentiable.  The derivative is $fprime_n05 .</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>For <m>a=0</m>, the secant slopes are:
</p>
<p>

<m>h=1: $slope_0_1 </m>, <m>h= -1: $slope_0_n1 </m>
</p>
<p>

<m>h=0.1: $slope_0_01 </m>, <m>h= -0.1: $slope_0_n01 </m>
</p>
<p>

<m>h=0.01: $slope_0_001 </m>, <m>h= -0.01: $slope_0_n001 </m></p>

<p>The derivative does not exist at <m>a=0</m>, i.e., the function is not differentiable.</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
The graph of <m>f</m> ($absRay1.styleDescription function), <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m> ($derivThru1.styleDescription function) and the non-differentiable point of <m>f</m> (red square):

<graph size="medium" xmin="-4.5" xmax="4.5" ymin="-4.5" ymax="4.5" showNavigation="false">

<point fixed="true" styleNumber="3">(0,0)</point>
<point fixed="true" styleNumber="3">(1,1)</point>
<point fixed="true" styleNumber="3">(-1,1)</point>
<ray fixed="true" endpoint="(0,0)" through="(1,1)" styleNumber="3" />
<ray fixed="true" endpoint="(0,0)" through="(-1,1)" styleNumber="3" /> 

<endpoint fixed="true" open="true">(0,1)</endpoint>
<endpoint fixed="true" open="true">(0,-1)</endpoint>
<point fixed="true">(3,1)</point>
<point fixed="true">(-3,-1)</point>
<ray fixed="true" endpoint="(0,1)" through="(3,1)" />
<ray fixed="true" endpoint="(0,-1)" through="(-3,-1)" />

<point fixed="true" styleNumber="2">(0,0)</point>

</graph>
</exercise>

</solution>


</problem>